<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kemal al-Din Husayn Bey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kemal al-Din Husayn Bey was the last important ruler of the Hamidid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egirdir">Eğirdir</a>. Unable to resist the rising Ottoman state, he sold several of his towns, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beysehir">Beyşehir</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksehir">Akşehir</a>, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-i">Murad I</a> in 1374. The remaining Hamidid lands were annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a> in 1391, making the beylik one of the first Turkish principalities absorbed peacefully by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p></div>
